<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Tahir ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Tahir ibn Muhammad was the founder of the Hazaraspid dynasty of Luristan in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. A Kurdish or Lur commander in the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salghurids">Salghurid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a>, he was sent around 1148 to subdue the region and made himself its ruler. His descendants governed Greater Luristan, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> mountains, for nearly three centuries.</p></div>
